{number: 96}
{title: Leaning on the Everlasting Arms}
{key: Ab}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Ab] What a fellowship, what a joy divine,
Leaning on the ever-[Eb7] lasting arms;
What a [Ab] blessedness, what a peace is mine,
Leaning on the ever-[Eb7] lasting [Ab] arms.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Ab] Leaning, [Db] leaning,
Safe and secure from [Eb7] all alarms;
[Ab] Leaning, [Db] leaning,
Leaning on the [Eb7] everlasting [Ab] arms.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
O how [Ab] sweet to walk in this pilgrim way,
Leaning on the ever-[Eb7] lasting arms;
O how [Ab] bright the path grows from day to day,
Leaning on the ever-[Eb7] lasting [Ab] arms.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
What have [Ab] I to dread, what have I to fear,
Leaning on the ever-[Eb7] lasting arms?
I have [Ab] blessed peace with my Lord so near,
Leaning on the ever-[Eb7] lasting [Ab] arms.
{end_of_verse}
